cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this study, please cite it as below."
title: "Do Kalshi prices match what happened? An actual-versus-expected study of prediction-market prices"
type: software
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-23
authors:
  - family-names: Hong
    given-names: Harrison
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24177577
repository-code: "https://github.com/HarrisonHong21/kalshi-actual-vs-expected"
abstract: >-
  An actual-versus-expected study of 24,903 settled Kalshi NFL and NBA player-prop
  contracts from 125 games and 6,113 graded sportsbook props (5 October to 19 November
  2026). Compares each price's implied chance with what happened, with game-cluster
  bootstrap intervals, a credibility standard, and a decomposition of a hypothetical
  buy-at-the-ask return into spread, fees and midpoint error. Also tests the app's
  Kalshi buying rules in sample and in frozen paper trials, pick'em lines, an old
  projection model and the book curve's far tails. Back-tests and paper trades only;
  not betting advice.
keywords:
  - prediction markets
  - calibration
  - actual versus expected
  - bootstrap
  - Kalshi
